# dispenser: an imaginary benchtop fluid dispenser / light pick-and-place,
# 600 x 400 mm, retrofitted with stmbl. One Y motor (an ironless Baldor
# LMCF06E) drives the bridge from one side; the other side runs on an
# idler rail with its own scale. An LMCF04C moves the head (a dispensing
# valve and a camera) along the bridge. Aluminium extrusion frame on rubber
# feet on an ordinary bench: the frame moves. Numbers are made up.
#@dynwiz 20000 20000 1000
drive y1 dispenser_y.conf ../sim.txt 60.96
drive y2 none
drive x dispenser_x.conf ../sim.txt 60.96
origin 300 200
stroke -5 405 -5 605
frame 90 4.5 7 6 8 0.08
rails 0.75
bridge 6.5 0.3
carriage 1.8 0.004
# with one motor the bridge's yaw is held by the guide blocks alone
racking 1.5e5 0.03
head 1.2 0.002 110 140 85 0.04
guidey 8 10
guidey2 5 6
guidex 4 5
# the drives' own 3 x 470 uF and a small brake chopper: at 2 g braking
# pumped the bus over the drives' 380 V
bus 1410 230 1.0 360 47
home 300 200
